# scroll_big.pixels -- frozen frame-hash baseline for tests/scroll_big_test.ast (v2.7.1).
# Generated by running scroll_big_test under aster-fixed (md5 86234516...),
# 2026-11-15: SCROLLBIGHASH -1859998762 (twice in one run, twice across
# runs, output byte-identical). The test runs a ScrollView at the real
# device resolution 1216x2688 (user's REDMAGIC phone, 520 dpi); the hash
# is the post-drag blit frame (off=180); PIXELCHECK asserts it equals a
# forced full repaint in the same run.
# v2.7.1 fixed the framebuffer-cap root cause this test pins: the old
# single i32[1048576] framebuffer could not hold 1216x2688 = 3268608 px,
# so fb_fits was always false on device, blit never engaged (fail 2),
# and every scroll frame was a full re-raster (20-47 ms). The buffer is
# now 8 chunks x 1M i32, row-aligned; the test asserts 5/5 drag steps
# blit (k>=2), miss/evict 0, and pixel equality with full repaint.
# The fake window bitmap is mmap'd by fake_set_win_size (a single Aster
# global array cannot hold 3268608 elements either).
# Re-pin only when the scene or the rendering legitimately changes.
SCROLLBIGHASH -1859998762
